(11103,'Set to %none to disable inheritance of the parent value and prevent the output of this metatag entirely.','','11.4.10'),
(11104,'The text to display in the title bar of a visitor\'s web browser when they view this page. This meta tag may also be used as the title of the page when a visitor bookmarks or favorites this page, or as the page title in a search engine result. It is common to append \'[site:name]\' to the end of this, so the site\'s name is automatically added. It is recommended that the title is no greater than 55 - 65 characters long, including spaces.','','11.4.10'),
(11105,'A brief and concise summary of the page\'s content that is a maximum of 160 characters in length. The description meta tag may be used by search engines to display a snippet about the page in search results.','','11.4.10'),
(11106,'A brief and concise summary of the page\'s content, preferably 150 characters or less. Where as the description meta tag may be used by search engines to display a snippet about the page in search results, the abstract tag may be used to archive a summary about the page. This meta tag is <em>no longer</em> supported by major search engines.','','11.4.10'),
(11107,'A comma-separated list of keywords about the page. This meta tag is <em>no longer</em> supported by most search engines.','','11.4.10'),
(11108,'A location\'s two-letter international country code, with an optional two-letter region, e.g. \'US-NH\' for New Hampshire in the USA.','','11.4.10'),
(11109,'Geo-spatial information in \'latitude, longitude\' format, e.g. \'50.167958, -97.133185\'; <a href=\'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ICBM_address\' aria-label=\'see Wikipedia for details on ICBM addresses\'>see Wikipedia for details</a>.','','11.4.10'),
(11110,'A location\'s formal name.','','11.4.10'),
(11111,'Geo-spatial information in \'latitude; longitude\' format, e.g. \'50.167958; -97.133185\'; <a href=\'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geographic_coordinate_system\' aria-label=\'see Wikipedia for details on the geographic coordinate system\'>see Wikipedia for details</a>.','','11.4.10'),
(11112,'A brief URL, often created by a URL shortening service.','','11.4.10'),
(11113,'A link to the preferred page location or URL of the content of this page, to help eliminate duplicate content penalties from search engines.','','11.4.10'),
(11114,'Used for paginated content by providing URL with rel=\'prev\' link.','','11.4.10'),
(11115,'Used for paginated content by providing URL with rel=\'next\' link.','','11.4.10'),
(11116,'Define the author of a page.','','11.4.10'),
(11117,'This will be able to extract the URL from an image field if the field is configured properly.','','11.4.10'),
(11118,'An image associated with this page, for use as a thumbnail in social networks and other services.','','11.4.10'),
(11119,'Used to indicate the URL that broke the story, and can link to either an internal URL or an external source. If the full URL is not known it is acceptable to use a partial URL or just the domain name.','','11.4.10'),
(11120,'Describes the name and version number of the software or publishing tool used to create the page.','','11.4.10'),
(11121,'Details about intellectual property, such as copyright or trademarks; does not automatically protect the site\'s content or intellectual property.','','11.4.10'),
(11122,'Used to rate content for audience appropriateness. This tag has little known influence on search engine rankings, but can be used by browsers, browser extensions, and apps. The <a href=\'https://www.metatags.org/meta_name_rating\'>most common options</a> are general, mature, restricted, 14 years, safe for kids. If you follow the <a href=\'https://www.rtalabel.org/index.php?content=howto\'>RTA Documentation</a> you should enter RTA-5042-1996-1400-1577-RTA','','11.4.10'),
(11123,'This meta tag communicates with Google. There are currently two directives supported: \'nositelinkssearchbox\' to not to show the sitelinks search box, and \'notranslate\' to ask Google not to offer a translation of the page. Both options may be added, just separate them with a comma. See <a href=\'https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/79812?hl=en\'>meta tags that Google understands</a> for further details.','','11.4.10'),
(11124,'The number of seconds to wait before refreshing the page. May also force redirect to another page using the format \'5; url=https://example.com/\', which would be triggered after five seconds.','','11.4.10'),
(11125,'<a href=\'https://www.metatags.org/meta_http_equiv_set_cookie\'>Sets a cookie</a> on the visitor\'s browser. Can be in either NAME=VALUE format, or a more verbose format including the path and expiration date; see the link for full details on the syntax.','','11.4.10'),
(11126,'Tell search engines when to index the page again. Very few search engines support this tag, it is more useful to use an <a href=\'https://www.drupal.org/project/xmlsitemap\'>XML Sitemap</a> file.','','11.4.10'),
(11127,'Used to control whether a browser caches a specific page locally. Not commonly used. Should be used in conjunction with the Pragma meta tag.','','11.4.10'),
(11128,'Control when the browser\'s internal cache of the current page should expire. The date must to be an <a href=\'https://www.csgnetwork.com/timerfc1123calc.html\'>RFC-1123</a>-compliant date string that is represented in Greenwich Mean Time (GMT), e.g. \'Thu, 01 Sep 2016 00:12:56 GMT\'. Set to \'0\' to stop the page being cached entirely.','','11.4.10'),
(11129,'Used to control whether a browser caches a specific page locally. Not commonly used. Should be used in conjunction with the Cache-Control meta tag.','','11.4.10'),
(11130,'The word that appears before the content\'s title in a sentence. The default ignores this value, the \'Automatic\' value should be sufficient if this is actually needed.','','11.4.10'),
(11131,'A human-readable name for the site, e.g., <em>IMDb</em>.','','11.4.10'),
(11132,'The type of the content, e.g., <em>movie</em>.','','11.4.10'),
(11133,'Preferred page location or URL to help eliminate duplicate content for search engines, e.g., <em>https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0117500/</em>.','','11.4.10'),
(11134,'The title of the content, e.g., <em>The Rock</em>.','','11.4.10'),
(11135,'A one to two sentence description of the content.','','11.4.10'),
(11136,'Multiple values may be used, separated by `:delimiter`. Note: Tokens that return multiple values will be handled automatically.','','11.4.10'),
(11137,'The URL of an image which should represent the content. The image must be at least 200 x 200 pixels in size; 600 x 316 pixels is a recommended minimum size, and for best results use an image least 1200 x 630 pixels in size. Supports PNG, JPEG and GIF formats. Should not be used if og:image:url is used. Note: if multiple images are added many services (e.g. Facebook) will default to the largest image, not specifically the first one.','','11.4.10'),
(11138,'The URL of an video which should represent the content. For best results use a source that is at least 1200 x 630 pixels in size, but at least 600 x 316 pixels is a recommended minimum. Object types supported include video.episode, video.movie, video.other, and video.tv_show.','','11.4.10'),
(11139,'A alternative version of og:image and has exactly the same requirements; only one needs to be used.','','11.4.10'),
(11140,'Any URLs which start with \"http://\" will be converted to \"https://\".','','11.4.10'),
(11141,'The secure URL (HTTPS) of an video which should represent the content.','','11.4.10'),
(11142,'The secure URL (HTTPS) of an image which should represent the content. The image must be at least 200 x 200 pixels in size; 600 x 316 pixels is a recommended minimum size, and for best results use an image least 1200 x 630 pixels in size. Supports PNG, JPEG and GIF formats.','','11.4.10'),
(11143,'The type of video referenced above. Should be either  video.episode, video.movie, video.other, and video.tv_show. Note: there should be one value for each video, and having more than there are videos may cause problems.','','11.4.10'),
(11144,'The type of image referenced above. Should be either \'image/gif\' for a GIF image, \'image/jpeg\' for a JPG/JPEG image, or \'image/png\' for a PNG image. Note: there should be one value for each image, and having more than there are images may cause problems.','','11.4.10'),
(11145,'The width of the above image(s). Note: if both the unsecured and secured images are provided, they should both be the same size.','','11.4.10'),
(11146,'The height of the above video(s). Note: if both the unsecured and secured videos are provided, they should both be the same size.','','11.4.10'),
(11147,'The height of the above image(s). Note: if both the unsecured and secured images are provided, they should both be the same size.','','11.4.10'),
(11148,'The length of the video in seconds','','11.4.10'),
(11149,'A description of what is in the image, not a caption. If the page specifies an og:image it should specify og:image:alt.','','11.4.10'),
(11150,'The date this content was last modified, with an optional time value. Needs to be in <a href=\'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601\'>ISO 8601</a> format. Can be the same as the \'Article modification date\' tag.','','11.4.10'),
(11151,'URLs to related content','','11.4.10'),
(11152,'The locale these tags are marked up in, must be in the format language_TERRITORY. Default is \'en_US\'.','','11.4.10'),
(11153,'Other locales this content is available in, must be in the format language_TERRITORY, e.g. \'fr_FR\'.','','11.4.10'),
(11154,'The fediverse @username for the content creator / author for this page, including the first @ symbol.','','11.4.10'),
(11155,'Links an article to an author\'s Facebook profile, should be either URLs to the author\'s profile page or their Facebook profile IDs.','','11.4.10'),
(11156,'Links an article to a publisher\'s Facebook page.','','11.4.10'),
(11157,'The primary section of this website the content belongs to.','','11.4.10'),
(11158,'Appropriate keywords for this content.','','11.4.10'),
(11159,'The date this content was published on, with an optional time value. Needs to be in <a href=\'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601\'>ISO 8601</a> format.','','11.4.10'),
(11160,'The date this content was last modified, with an optional time value. Needs to be in <a href=\'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601\'>ISO 8601</a> format.','','11.4.10'),
(11161,'The date this content will expire, with an optional time value. Needs to be in <a href=\'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_8601\'>ISO 8601</a> format.','','11.4.10'),
(11162,'Links a book to an author\'s Facebook profile, should be either URLs to the author\'s profile page or their Facebook profile IDs.','','11.4.10'),
(11163,'The Book\'s ISBN','','11.4.10'),
